      "proof_review": {
        "reviewed": true,
        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "The complete selected author proof is Theorem8.3 first equation restricted to r=1 and origin strictly interior, giving Theorem5.10 first equation via Remark6.4. The reduced consistent bipartite torus dimer, chosen type-I zigzag z, edge E with outer normal v=[z], w=-v, hmin=-1, and deformation p1=hmax=length(z)/2-1 are fixed exactly by Settings6.1 and8.1. The oriented primitive factor is F=conv{0,h(Pzprime,Pz)} from Setting7.8, with origins aligned along unchanged y-edges. Full local supports3.9–3.16, nondegeneracy7.1, trajectories7.2–7.4 and slopes7.5–7.9 are included. The r=1 branch has no bypasses or removal step by Remark6.4; it does not depend on the extended general cleanup construction. Prior properly-ordered dimer and corner-cutting results are explicitly identified author background. The polygon polar mutation correspondence5.7 is already attributed to the prior ACGK Proposition4; its local presentation is also preserved. Proof diagrams on physical page33 were visually checked against the matching construction. No inverse-mutation, hexagonal/rectangular variant, helper lemma or zag branch is separately counted."
      },
